.TH COWBOY\-BANNER 1 "2026" "cowboy-banner 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cowboy\-banner \- ASCII/Unicode art banner printed at shell startup
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cowboy\-banner
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints a random 76x24 ASCII/Unicode picture with a greeting and a random
saying. The theme is picked by
.BR COWBOY_THEME ,
the picture inside the theme is random and never repeats the one from the
previous shell, unless the theme has only a single picture.
.PP
Runs automatically from
.IR ~/.bashrc ,
.I ~/.zshrc
and the PowerShell profile (see
.IR cowboy\-banner.install ).
.SS Themes
.TP
.B wildwest
Дикий Запад, 4 картинки (default)
.TP
.B space
Космос, 2 картинки
.TP
.B cyber
Киберпанк, 2 картинки
.TP
.B ocean
Океан, 2 картинки
.TP
.B any
случайная тема при каждом запуске
.TP
.B menu
показать меню тем
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B COWBOY_THEME
wildwest (default), space, cyber, ocean, any, menu.
.TP
.B COWBOY_BANNER
unset or empty - draw the picture; \fBmenu\fR (\fBoff\fR) - theme menu;
\fBnone\fR - print nothing; \fBplain\fR, \fBascii\fR - picture without color.
.TP
.B COWBOY_CMD
alias for COWBOY_BANNER, in case the latter name is already taken.
.TP
.B COWBOY_HINT
\fBon\fR, \fB1\fR, \fByes\fR, \fBtrue\fR - show the hint line and the
\fB[theme]\fR tag under the picture. Off by default.
.TP
.B COWBOY_ALWAYS
\fB1\fR - print even when stdout is not a terminal (useful in scripts
and tests).
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
if set, colors are disabled (see https://no-color.org).
.TP
.B COWBOY_ROOT
directory with the art and data, default /usr/share/cowboy-banner.
.SH EXAMPLES
Show the theme menu:
.PP
.RS
COWBOY_BANNER=menu cowboy\-banner
.RE
.PP
Same, but picture without color:
.PP
.RS
COWBOY_BANNER=plain cowboy\-banner
.RE
.PP
Switch theme for good (bash):
.PP
.RS
echo 'export COWBOY_THEME=ocean' >> ~/.bashrc
.RE
.PP
Switch theme for good (PowerShell):
.PP
.RS
pwsh -c '$env:COWBOY_THEME = "ocean"'
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/cowboy-banner
the script itself
.TP
.I /usr/share/cowboy-banner/art
10 pre-rendered pictures with ANSI colors
.TP
.I /usr/share/cowboy-banner/data
greetings, sayings and scene lists
.TP
.I /usr/share/cowboy-banner/profile.ps1
PowerShell version
.TP
.I ~/.bashrc, ~/.zshrc, ~/.config/powershell/Microsoft.PowerShell_profile.ps1
where the banner is started
.TP
.I ${XDG_RUNTIME_DIR:-/tmp}/cowboy-banner.state
last shown picture, so it does not repeat
.SH SEE ALSO
The README in /usr/share/doc/cowboy-banner.
